      "ui": {
        "label": "MiniMax-H3 References",
        "attribution": "Powered by MiniMax H3",
        "description": "The reference-conditioned half of MiniMax-H3: give it up to 9 images, 3 video clips and 3 audio clips (12 files in total) and it renders a new clip — with synchronized stereo audio — that carries those subjects, motions and voices. It uses a second checkpoint from the same family, so installing it adds the reference DiT alongside whatever text-to-video tiers you already have; the text encoder and both VAEs are shared and download only once. It runs through native MLX on Apple Silicon and Candle/CUDA on Windows and Linux. Same open-weights caveats as MiniMax-H3, and they are not small: the hosted prompt-understanding front end (H3-Context-IR) and the 2K in-context upscaler (H3-Regenerate-2K) are unreleased, so prompt adherence differs from the Hailuo API and 2K is not reachable from these weights; attention runs dense by default. Optional Veda sparse attention uses the managed predictor and falls back to dense when it cannot run; the shortest dense clip at the default 1344x768 canvas is about a two-hour render. There is no guidance scale and no negative prompt. Clips come in the same fourteen fixed lengths between 5.17s and 14.38s — 15s is refused rather than shortened — and there is no still-image mode.",
        "recommendedFor": [
          "reference_to_video"
        ],
        "durationHint": "Same fourteen clip lengths as MiniMax-H3, 5.17s to 14.38s at 24fps — nothing in between renders and 15s is refused rather than shortened to 14.38s — and the same canvas-dominated cost, so start at 576x320.",
